1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:10,644
EU regulators say Meta may have broken the Digital Services Act because Facebook and Instagram use designs that keep people scrolling for too long.

2
00:00:10,594 --> 00:00:18,035
The Verge reports that autoplay, infinite scroll and recommendation systems are under scrutiny.

3
00:00:18,035 --> 00:00:26,623
Meta can respond, but the case could force app changes and strengthen Europe's wider push to protect young users online.

